   "top": {
    "Magoksa Temple is situated on Taehwasan Mountain in Gongju, Chungcheongnam-do Province. The temple site has long been called the “most blessed land of the East” and considered a propitious site. The landscape looks most beautiful in the springtime out of all four seasons.": 1,
    "The temple is also famous as a place of refuge for Baekbeom Kim Gu, who was a prominent independence activist in the Japanese occupation period. Kim Gu escaped from Incheon Prison, where he had been imprisoned for the murder of a Japanese military officer, who had taken part in the assassination of Empress Myeongseong. After his escape, he found refuge at Magoksa Temple.": 1,
    "“Daeungbojeon” means a “house where Shakyamuni Buddha is enshrined.” The Daeungbojeon Hall of Magoksa temple is a cultural asset that has been designated as a treasure. ": 1,
    "Daeungbojeon Hall, which is the main hall of Magoksa Temple, was rebuilt in 1788. Inside, a statue of Vairocana Buddha, representing the embodiment of the truth, is enshrined in such a way that it faces the east from the west side of the building. ": 1,
    "Yeongsanjeon Hall is known to be a place where there is an accumulation of energy from Gunwangdae, which is said to instill benevolence among ministers and bravery among soldiers. Many Buddhists come here to pray to the Buddha, hoping to see competent individuals leading the nation to greatness. As the oldest building at the Magoksa Temple site, it was repaid in 1650.": 1,
    "Haetalmun is the main gate of Magoksa Temple, past which you can escape the secular world and enter the Dharma realm.": 1,
    "Cheonwangmun is the second gate, where there paintings of the four maharajas, who guard the four quarters of heaven and the Buddha-dharma.": 1,
    "The five-story stone pagoda is called either Dabotap or Geumap. Legend has it that the stone pagoda has the power to prevent a nationwide wide for three days. ": 1,
    "Address: 966 Magoksa-ro, Sagok-myeon, Gongju-si, Chungcheongnam-do (567 Unam-ri) \nTel: 041-841-6221\nHours of operation: Open year-round \nAdmission: Adult – 3,000 won / Youth – 1,500 / Free for military officers, the disabled, and seniors \nMain facilities: Taehwaseonwon, Yeongsanjeon, Hongseongnu, etc. ": 1,
    "Gongju Hanok Village is comprised of new hanok, or traditional Korean houses, which have been designed to allow visitors to experience gudeuljang, which is a flat stone used in the traditional Korean floor heating system. Nearby the village, you can experience Baekje culture through a wide range of activities and programs, take a stroll along the Dulle-gil Trail of the village, or rent a bicycle for a cycling tour of the cultural heritage sites of the small town and old town areas.": 1
   },
